/*!
 * Slaide viewer — interface language (English source, German alternative).
 *
 * The viewer's chrome, the Pro editor, the inspector and Theme Studio all live in ONE document
 * (the ribbon is injected into the rendered deck), so one pass over the DOM translates every one
 * of them and no widget has to know about languages.
 *
 * Keyed by the ENGLISH SOURCE STRING: an untranslated string still renders correctly, and a call
 * site reads as the sentence it shows.
 *
 * NEVER translated: the deck itself (`.sl-slide`, wherever it is cloned), speaker notes, the
 * user's own document title, and data values — font names, layout names, transition names,
 * master token names, style classes.
 *
 * The HOSTED web editor does not load this file: that page runs the server's own pass, and two
 * passes would fight over the same nodes.
 *
 * Generated from the same German the hosted app uses — do not hand-edit one without the other.
 */
